# Project structure

Keep the tree predictable. Put new code in the right folder — do not invent parallel trees.

```
src/
  app/                 # Next.js App Router only (pages + route handlers)
    api/               # HTTP API — mirrors former Python server endpoints
    layout.tsx         # fonts, Providers, dark theme shell
    page.tsx           # entry — compose feature components, no business UI here
  components/
    ui/                # shadcn primitives ONLY (CLI-managed; prefer `npx shadcn add`)
    editor/            # feature UI modules (toolbar, sidebar, inspector, panes)
      dialogs/         # one file per modal flow (*Dialog.tsx)
    providers.tsx      # app-wide client providers (Tooltip, Toaster, …)
  hooks/               # reusable React hooks (no JSX layout)
  lib/
    plan/              # OE plan domain (model, validator, run, colors, types)
    server/            # Node-only FS / settings / schema / proxy helpers
    api.ts             # browser fetch helpers
    utils.ts           # cn() and shared client utils
  store/               # Zustand stores
data/                  # schema-cache.json (generated)
settings.json          # local settings (gitignored); settings.example.json committed
```

## Placement rules

- **Route handlers** → `src/app/api/**/route.ts`. Shared logic → `src/lib/server/`.
- **Plan domain logic** (normalize, edges, validate, upsert/run) → `src/lib/plan/`. Never duplicate in components.
- **Reusable visuals** → `src/components/ui/` via shadcn CLI, or thin wrappers in `src/components/editor/`.
- **Editor regions** → `src/components/editor/*` (sidebar, inspector, graph panel, json pane, toolbar).
- **Modals** → `src/components/editor/dialogs/*Dialog.tsx` (compose `AppDialog`).
- **`PlanEditor.tsx`** = orchestration only (state + compose modules). No large panel/modal JSX.
- **Do not** put business logic in `src/components/ui/`.
- **Do not** add one-off styled `div`/`button`/`input` when a `ui/*` primitive exists.
- Components are **configurable** (`className` + props) and **desktop-first adaptive** — see `modular-ui.mdc`.
